Spec: HTTP Server
Purpose: Bereitstellung der HTTP REST API, Delegation der Workflows an den Scheduler, und Auslieferung von statischen Frontend-Assets via Tera-Templating.

Structure:
  ./specs/
  ./src/
  ./templates/
  ./static/

Owns:
  ./**

References:
  ./specs/architecture.sdd
  ./specs/tech_spec.sdd
  ./specs/api_spec.sdd
  ./specs/prd.sdd

Must:
  The server must serve static assets (HTML, JS, Images) from a configurable or dedicated static directory.
  The server must integrate the Tera templating engine for dynamic HTML rendering.
  The server must deliver an `index.html` template when the root `/` endpoint is accessed.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Implement Request-ID (UUID) middleware to generate and inject `X-Request-ID` header and `meta.request_id` into all JSON responses.
  [x] #2 Pass the generated Request-ID via UDS IPC payloads to IAM and Scheduler servers for distributed tracing.
  [x] #3 Eliminate remaining mock data (e.g. mock backup version, mock key rotation count) in admin.rs.
  [x] #32.1 Add `mitm_dir` to `mitm_common::config::DBConfig`, populated by `MITM_DIR` ENV (fallback: current executable's directory).
  [x] #32.2 Add `tera` and `tower-http` (with `fs` feature) dependencies to `Cargo.toml`.
  [x] #32.3 Create a thread-safe `Tera` engine in `AppState` initialized with `<MITM_DIR>/html/templates/**/*`.
  [x] #32.4 Add `ServeDir` as a fallback service in `configure_routes` to serve static assets from `<MITM_DIR>/html/public`.
  [x] #32.5 Implement a handler for `GET /` that renders `index.html` via Tera.
  [x] #32.6 Update `auth_middleware` to bypass authentication for any path that does not start with `/admin`, making the frontend and static assets public.
